cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use caroli in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "caroli: a Rust toolbox for electronic transport in materials"
abstract: >-
  caroli builds tight-binding systems (lattices, geometry, disorder, magnetic fields) and computes
  their electronic properties: two- and multi-terminal transport with Green's functions (nested
  dissection, recursive Green's functions, lead modes), non-equilibrium steady states (Keldysh),
  the self-consistent Born approximation, the kernel polynomial method and time evolution, on all
  the CPU cores and, for some kernels, on the GPU.
authors:
  - family-names: Demion
    given-names: Arnaud
type: software
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/Arnwald/caroli"
keywords:
  - quantum transport
  - tight-binding
  - Green's functions
  - topological insulators
  - graphene
  - Rust
